# BOND utilities — bond-utilities (Q-BRANCH) manuscript configuration

This is the richer, copy-and-customize reference copy of `config.yaml` for the
bond-utilities package. Every `{{TOKEN}}` in the manuscript is computed from
this file (or derived deterministically from it) by
`src/bond_utilities/manuscript_variables.py`.

```yaml
paper:
  title: "Q-Branch Field Utility Library"
  subtitle: "Cipher, Codename, Clock, Randomness, and Provenance Primitives for Mission Operations"
  version: "0.2.0"
  date: "2026-08-04"

authors:
  - name: "Daniel Ari Friedman"
    orcid: "0000-0001-6232-9096"
    email: "daniel@activeinference.institute"
    affiliation: "Active Inference Institute"
    corresponding: true

keywords:
  - "classical ciphers"
  - "cryptanalysis"
  - "deterministic codenames"
  - "mission scheduling"
  - "seeded randomness"
  - "provenance records"

metadata:
  license: "MIT"
  language: "en"

# Mission parameters — every {{TOKEN}} is computed from this section.
mission:
  codename: "Q-BRANCH"            # {{MISSION_CODENAME}}
  default_seed: 20260804          # {{CONFIG_DEFAULT_SEED}}
  num_codenames: 6                # {{CONFIG_NUM_CODENAMES}}
  schedule:                       # {{RESULT_WINDOW_HOURS}}
    start: "2026-08-04T00:00:00Z"     # {{CONFIG_SCHEDULE_START}}
    end:   "2026-08-10T00:00:00Z"     # {{CONFIG_SCHEDULE_END}}
  # A secondary window inside the primary schedule; {{RESULT_OVERLAP_HOURS}}
  # is the overlap of the two windows.
  overlap_window:
    start: "2026-08-06T12:00:00Z"
    end:   "2026-08-08T12:00:00Z"

testing:
  max_test_failures: 0
```

## Editing protocol

1. Change a value in `config.yaml` (not here).
2. Re-run `uv run python scripts/z_generate_manuscript_variables.py` to
   regenerate `output/data/manuscript_variables.json` and both figures
   (`output/figures/mission_schedule.png`, `output/figures/letter_frequency.png`).
3. Re-render the manuscript if the render pipeline is wired.
4. The live cross-reference test
   `tests/test_manuscript_variables.py::TestManuscriptCrossReference` fails
   if any `{{TOKEN}}` in `manuscript/[0-9]*.md` is not produced by
   `generate_variables()`.
